{"title":"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d2c338f8d129687a4c356073fea88cc08aa2e1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=t^{1/(t-1)}$\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/9910159ddd134088d3c74d8de52994cb5e41186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=t^{t/(t-1)},t&gt;0,t \\ne 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" />, a relation between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab48c833a7f189dd91f3d1f70f6b6ee50fd5719b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } y^x=x^{1/y}\\quad \\text{(B) } y^{1/x}=x^{y}\\quad \\text{(C) } y^x=x^y\\quad \\text{(D) } x^x=y^y\\quad \\text{(E) none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"585\" height=\"22\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/2/6c240b39d84768470be7a72674d0acf93c133e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 2$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> and test each expression (if the relation works, then both sides are equal).  After testing, options A, B, and D are out, but for option C, both sides are equal.  To check that C is a valid option, substitute the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and use exponent properties.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c113d8ef32789e02ed726743d4f7ba59dcc492.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^y = (t^{\\frac{1}{t-1}})^{t^{\\frac{t}{t-1}}} = t^{\\frac{1}{t-1} \\cdot t^{\\frac{t}{t-1}}}\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"27\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f0118bdf3d5b15d40f7b78102729d3729e5e225.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^x = (t^{\\frac{t}{t-1}})^{t^{\\frac{1}{t-1}}} = t^{\\frac{t}{t-1} \\cdot t^{\\frac{1}{t-1}}}\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"28\" />\nIn the second equation, the exponent can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c6799c1fadd57f1afeae40cd2ef482e6b721efbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{t-1} \\cdot t \\cdot t^{\\frac{1}{t-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"87\" height=\"24\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0ce41754085e00ffd5d174661c3eb267c56b37e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{t-1}{t-1} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"58\" height=\"21\" />, the exponent can be simplified as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e551dd9014f08b72cb641b6129d4d522f3ed8bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{t-1} \\cdot t^{\\frac{t-1}{t-1}} \\cdot t^{\\frac{1}{t-1}} = \\tfrac{1}{t-1} \\cdot t^{\\frac{t}{t-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"205\" height=\"25\" />.  Since the base and exponent of both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9af910fe749481919573c0dd2b132118f19d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^y$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a71115e45c7ce99c5dea3da83f821c2360d3d925.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> are the same, we can confirm that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac09b8c4b30ba56801abf6e86ed3548e4807ce65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } y^x = x^y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"109\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME\" title=\"1969 AHSME\">1969 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1969 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1969\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br